    "originalFinding": "**R2A-F03 \u2014 Informational.** Producer-recorded local DLL hashes (e.g. `Gagamba.Execution.dll` `766f2bfc\u2026`) did not reproduce byte-identically on my rebuild (same 137,728-byte size, different hash). The evidence explicitly scopes these as \"not package or deployment qualification\"; the reproduction criterion \u2014 test outcomes \u2014 did reproduce. No claim is invalidated.\r\n\r\n",
    "originalDisposition": "| R2A-F03 | Locally rebuilt DLL bytes were not byte-identical despite matching test outcomes | **ACCEPT AS DISCLOSED** | No binary reproducibility or deployment qualification claim is accepted; the producer's own non-qualification scoping of local DLL hashes stands. No immediate remediation is required. Test-reproducibility versus binary-reproducibility is kept distinct in RC2A-02 evidence rules (\u00a73, E4) |",
